Subject: [PATCH 1/7] CMake: -ffloat-store only for 32-bit x86 doing float maths on the x87

VibeSDR patch for FAAD2 2.11.3 (the plain build VibeServer links for DAB+ audio, libfaad_dab.a). GPL-2.0-or-later,
as FAAD2. Written for VibeSDR, 2026-10-26; applied by vibeserver/linux/build-deps.sh and vibeserver/mac/build-deps.sh
in the order of faad2-patches/series. Measured on real off-air DAB+ unit logs (HE-AAC v2, 21 logs, 1909 s):
output against stock FAAD2 2.11.3 built with its own flags — see each header for the figures.

FAAD2's CMakeLists adds -ffloat-store for every GCC build. It exists for the x87, whose 80-bit registers could
otherwise change float results; on ARM, on x86-64 and on i386 built -mfpmath=sse it does nothing useful and forces
every float (and vector) temporary through the stack. On ARMv7 (the Raspberry Pi 2) that was most of the decoder's
instructions: with -funsafe-math-optimizations (build-deps.sh) the armhf guest instruction count for 59 s of an
HE-AAC v2 service falls from 3209 M (stock flags) to 1241 M with this patch alone; output against stock: max |diff|
1.6e-6, SNR 132.5 dB, level / third octaves / side-mid identical to 0.0001 dB. Kept for i386 without -mfpmath=sse.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -139,9 +139,13 @@
   )
 endif()
 
-if(CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "GNU")
+# VibeSDR (2026-10-26): -ffloat-store only where it does anything useful — 32-bit x86 doing float maths on the x87
+# (it keeps every float temporary in memory so x87's 80-bit registers cannot change results). Everywhere else (ARM,
+# x86-64, i386 with -mfpmath=sse) it only forces every float and vector temporary through the stack: on the Pi 2
+# (Cortex-A7) that was most of the stock decoder's instructions.
+if(CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "GNU" AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "^(i.86|x86)$" AND NOT CMAKE_C_FLAGS MATCHES "mfpmath=sse")
   list(APPEND FAAD_FLAGS -ffloat-store)
-endif()  # GCC
+endif()  # GCC, x87
 
 file(COPY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include/neaacdec.h
      DESTINATION ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/include)
